{% if part == "Vars" %}
{% endif %}
{% if part == "Doc" %}	DONE:
	- added the meta data from the real book.
	- put in the tunes structure.
	- put in the chords (real book).
	- added youtube performances (the real book refers to Gary Burton - 'Country Roads').
	TODO:
	- check the chords (real book).
	- put in the tune (real book). The book prints this tune as a two staff piano arrangement (melody in two and three note voicings with sixteenth note runs over a written out bass line) and the rhythms of the top line could not be read reliably from the handwritten page, so only the chords are typed for now.
	- put in the rubato intro (one free bar of piano chords with fermatas, no chord symbols) and the one bar bass fill that leads into the head.
	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	REMARKS:
	- the book marks the head 'Slow Funk'. It has a key signature of two flats.
	- the last bar of the head (marked Fine) has no chord symbol, only the same piano voicings as the intro; it is left empty here. In the solo section the book writes a repeat sign (Bb7) for that bar.
{% endif %}
{% if part == "ChordsReal" %}\chordmode {
	\startChords
	\startSong

	\myMark "A"
	\startPart
	\repeat volta 2 {
		bes1:7 | ees:7 | bes:7 | bes:7 | \myEndLine
		ees:7 | ees:7 | bes2:7 f:7 | bes:7 g:7 | \myEndLine
		ges1:7 | f:7 | bes:7 | s1 | \myEndLine
	}
	\endPart

	\myMark "Instr"
	\startPart
	\repeat volta 2 {
		bes1:7 | ees:7 | bes:7 | bes:7 | \myEndLine
		ees:7 | ees:7 | bes2:7 f:7 | bes:7 g:7 | \myEndLine
		ges1:7 | f:7 | bes:7 | bes:7 | \myEndLine
	}
	\endPart

	\endSong
	\endChords
}
{% endif %}
{% if part == "VoiceReal" %}{
	\tempo "Andante" 4 = 80
	\time 4/4
	\key bes \major

	% part "A"
	\repeat volta 2 {
		r1 | r1 | r1 | r1 |
		r1 | r1 | r1 | r1 |
		r1 | r1 | r1 | r1^\markup { \italic { Fine } } |
	}

	% part "Instr"
	\repeat volta 2 {
		r1^\markup { Solos } | r1 | r1 | r1 |
		r1 | r1 | r1 | r1 |
		r1 | r1 | r1 | r1 |
	}
}
{% endif %}
